  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved only 0.532 accuracy at 0.62 GPU hours, leaving substantial room for improvement. The single most impactful untested lever is whether multiprofile aggregation unlocks additional information beyond a single profile. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile (with the same scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l encoders and concat fusion) meaningfully improve validation accuracy? config_031 changes exactly one architectural dimension (single→multiprofile with avgpool aggregation), giving a clean controlled comparison against the baseline. I choose avgpool over transformer aggregation because it is cheaper and sufficient to establish whether multiprofile helps at all; if it does, a transformer-aggregation variant can be tested as a logical follow-up. Expected cost: roughly 1.5–2.5× the 0.62 GPU-hour baseline (≈1–1.5 GPU hours) due to processing multiple profiles per cell, still well within budget. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it resolves the largest source of uncertainty (profile-level information) while keeping the comparison clean and the cost moderate, preserving budget for subsequent encoder and aggregation refinements."
}

